      "claim": "Cyanidin-3-O-glucoside, a glycosylated polyphenol structurally analogous to the query flavone C-glucoside, reached brain tissue after intraperitoneal administration in mice, with brain levels peaking at approximately 3.5 nmol/g, demonstrating meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "Camellianin A, a flavonoid glycoside, yielded brain-detected camellianin B after intragastric administration in rats, directly showing that flavonoid glycosides can cross the blood-brain barrier after systemic dosing.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "Rutin, a quercetin glycoside, was detected in rat brain after oral administration of an E. senticosus extract, providing direct evidence that flavonoid O-glycosides achieve brain exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "Cyanidin-3-O-glucoside was the predominant anthocyanin detected in rat brain homogenates after dietary feeding, with brain content exceeding plasma content, confirming that glycosylated polyphenols can accumulate in the CNS.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "Intact cyanidin-3-galactoside was observed in pig brain after feeding, supporting the translational relevance of glycosylated polyphenol BBB crossing in a large-animal model.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple independent in vivo studies demonstrate that glycosylated polyphenols—anthocyanin glucosides/galactosides and flavonoid glycosides—cross the BBB and reach brain tissue after oral, IV, or IP administration in rodents, pigs, and humans. The query molecule, orientin (luteolin 8-C-glucoside), shares the key glycosylated polyphenol scaffold and is predicted to have meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain pharmacokinetic study of orientin itself is available; prediction relies on structurally analogous glycosylated flavonoids and anthocyanins.",
    "The exact contribution of efflux transporters or metabolites versus intact compound is not fully resolved for the query, though intact glycosides were detected in brain in the analogue records."
